  "title": "# Build: urgent-main-ci-green (Current profile) - URGENT ops fix Found by window-resize-fix (#278):…",
  "asked": "# Build: urgent-main-ci-green (Current profile) - URGENT ops fix Found by window-resize-fix (#278): CI on main is RED on three jobs unrelated to that fix: (1) a widget types check, (2) Molly's xlayout plugin has `opens: false` (a plugin manifest/check failure), (3) two Kotlin widget tests. Every PR fails on the same three, so auto-merge (auto-land-2) and the batch merge are stuck for everything. Brett's standing rule: fix broken stuff right away, tell him after. Assigned agent: whoever is free (router if on main; else **Earl the Ear**; record who). Register in the `current` profile (id `urgent-main-ci-green`) + banner entry. ## Do - s1 Read the latest failing main CI run (GitHub Actions via axHub github service or gh in the repo), get exact failures. - s2 Fix each at the root (correct code/manifest/test, not skipping or deleting tests). For the Kotlin widget tests: Android is on hold, but the tests are in CI - fix them properly; only if a fix needs real Android work, mark them with a documented, tracked skip and say so. - s3 Get main green; merge as a small PR right away (this is an ops fix that unblocks everything; still file a UI Review item only if UI changed). Then re-run CI on the open PRs waiting (#265 crew-retrain, #266 console-wake, #268 menu-scroll, #269 builds-one-page-done, #271 md-studio, #279) so they pick up green main (update from main if needed). - s4 Add a health@1 check: red banner item when main CI is red, with the failing job names and an Auto fix that queues an ops-fix job to a free agent. - s5 Report `_claude/builds/reports/urgent-main-ci-green.md`, THREADS, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
